{
  "title": "There is, there are",
  "kind": "grammar",
  "cefr": "A1",
  "estMinutes": 9,
  "intro": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Form"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "header": true,
      "rows": [
        [
          "—",
          "positive",
          "negative",
          "question"
        ],
        [
          "one thing",
          "There is (There's) a …",
          "There isn't a …",
          "Is there a …?"
        ],
        [
          "more things",
          "There are some …",
          "There aren't any …",
          "Are there any …?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "header": true,
      "rows": [
        [
          "question",
          "short answers"
        ],
        [
          "Is there a bank?",
          "Yes, there is. / No, there isn't."
        ],
        [
          "Are there any shops?",
          "Yes, there are. / No, there aren't."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Use"
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "title": "there is / there are",
      "points": [
        "We use it to say that something exists or is in a place.",
        "We usually say WHERE: There is a park near my house.",
        "There + is/are comes first; the thing comes after."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "title": "With a list",
      "points": [
        "Use is if the first thing is singular: There is a table and two chairs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "title": "How many …?",
      "points": [
        "How many rooms are there? — There are four."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. there is or it is?"
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "title": "Different meanings",
      "points": [
        "There is a cat in the garden. (new information: a cat exists there)",
        "It is black. (we already know the cat)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Be careful!"
    },
    {
      "type": "mistake",
      "wrong": "Is a bank near here.",
      "right": "There is a bank near here."
    },
    {
      "type": "mistake",
      "wrong": "There is three chairs.",
      "right": "There are three chairs."
    },
    {
      "type": "mistake",
      "wrong": "In my room there have a bed.",
      "right": "There is a bed in my room."
    }
  ],
